{"total_count":25385,"incomplete_results":false,"items":[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agora-Build/Atem/issues/81","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agora-Build/Atem","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agora-Build/Atem/issues/81/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agora-Build/Atem/issues/81/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agora-Build/Atem/issues/81/events","html_url":"https://github.com/Agora-Build/Atem/issues/81","id":5922252558,"node_id":"I_kwDORM5cZ88AAAABYP5nDg","number":81,"title":"Astation handoff: independent remote clients, staged approvals, rich chat","user":{"login":"guohai","id":436781,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQzNjc4MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/436781?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guohai","html_url":"https://github.com/guohai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guohai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guohai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guohai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guohai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guohai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guohai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guohai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guohai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guohai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":333,"created_at":"2026-10-19T10:32:51Z","updated_at":"2026-11-02T05:07:48Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"This is the latest Astation-to-Atem handoff for independent remote clients. Please review the joint contract decisions before implementing admission or emitting new signed push fields.\n\nSources:\n- Astation draft PR #58: https://github.com/Agora-Build/Astation/pull/58\n- Reviewed handoff snapshot: Astation commit a9e850a0a76e81b131697fe1ce8ee8fb076be108.\n- Remote/API design: https://github.com/Agora-Build/Astation/blob/a9e850a0a76e81b131697fe1ce8ee8fb076be108/designs/protocol/remote-agent-api.md\n- Signed push/scheduler proposal: https://github.com/Agora-Build/Astation/blob/a9e850a0a76e81b131697fe1ce8ee8fb076be108/designs/protocol/approval-push-proof.md\n- Current readable copies (VPN): https://truck.netbird.cloud:58310/protocol/remote-agent-api.md and https://truck.netbird.cloud:58310/protocol/approval-push-proof.md\n\n## Product requirements\n\n1. Mobile/native Astation connects independently to the original Atem host, whether Mac Astation is online or offline. Mac and mobile can view the same original agent sessions concurrently. The Atem host itself must remain running/reachable. Each controller has its own enrolled keys and attachment; no dependency on the Mac's local API or borrowed credentials.\n2. Keep r8 operation semantics: one terminal/control lease per agent session; prompt Send atomically acquires an unowned lease, and taking another holder requires confirmed expected-controller takeover. Approval answers and rule revocation are lease-free with control permission and the exact request/rule. Reading or approving on mobile must not disturb the Mac's lease. Reconnect never silently regains control.\n3. Use WSS first. A later Agora Signaling adapter may improve end-user connectivity, but must preserve endpoint proof, encryption, ordering, target/lease fencing and durable receipts. Verify runtime/platform and network support before enabling it. Whole-message responses are sufficient; token-by-token streaming is not required.\n4. Preserve rich response content. Existing text parts already carry Markdown; retain original source, typed tool/approval parts, IDs and ordering in live/history/API delivery. Mobile will render paragraphs, headings, bold/italic, highlighted links, lists, code blocks with highlighting/copy, and tables. Basic formatting needs no new host message type. Images/audio/PDF/files are separate capabilities and must not be implied by Markdown support.\n5. Approval live cards/events remain immediate. For an approval still pending and unexpired, initial OS push is due at 60 seconds from original creation; the reminder is due at 180 seconds, two more minutes later. Desktop defaults to both alerts; mobile registers to start at the reminder, so the relay does not send mobile's first OS alert. A desktop reminder is explicitly acceptable. No trusted desktop/mobile identity category is needed; use a small registered notification preference. App-only filtering is insufficient for OS alerts while mobile is suspended.\n6. Both escalation deadlines belong to the relay and do not depend on desktop connectivity or successful first delivery. Any authoritative answer/closure from Mac, mobile or the local terminal cancels remaining stages. Viewing a card/provider acknowledgment does not count as handled. Duplicates, catch-up and restart preserve deadlines. Expiry suppresses alerts; late taps fetch authoritative state. Deduplicate retries per stage without suppressing the desktop's intentional reminder.\n\n## Atem work and joint decisions\n\n- Resolve membership freshness/fork handling, principal kinds/wire versioning, exact signed formats and a reviewed secure channel, and reusable client-core ownership. Existing #70 any-manager nonce proof does not establish a bounded revocation guarantee when a removed manager can sign a withheld head. Section 9 remains the admission gate; the relay is never authoritative for identity or encryption/control state.\n- Agree an immutable signed original approval-creation timestamp (distinct from retry/event issue time), expiry and resolution ordering, clock validation and shared signature fixtures. Send opens/resolutions promptly; Atem does not wait 60/180 seconds or run escalation timers. Relay owns routing preferences, durable outbox, scheduling and provider delivery.\n- Enforce independent device/grant admission and revocation fences at effect boundaries, using existing r8 journal/recovery guarantees. Add multi-device/headless fixtures covering both clients online, Mac off/wake, reconnects, takeover races, approval answers while another holds control, and interrupted/duplicate submissions.\n- Provide representative Markdown/tool/approval messages for source-fidelity checks through history/reconnect. Rendering/UI and real APNs/FCM delivery checks remain Astation/platform work.\n\nThe remote routes, membership admission and authenticated staged push are proposals, not enabled product features. The agreed application baseline remains r8 at Atem 4f87bab1289848cb6a0da5707d2e7830eb5c057d. Astation has not edited or built an Atem checkout for this work. Astation owns implementation of relay/native clients; the Atem agent owns all host changes.\n\nLocal shared-memory publication was unavailable because the installed Atem CLI is unpaired. This issue provides a durable cross-repository handoff instead.\n\nGenerated with SMT <smt@agora.build>\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agora-Build/Atem/issues/81/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agora-Build/Atem/issues/81/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/BryceCurran86/PlanReader-3D/issues/2396","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/BryceCurran86/PlanReader-3D","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/BryceCurran86/PlanReader-3D/issues/2396/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/BryceCurran86/PlanReader-3D/issues/2396/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/BryceCurran86/PlanReader-3D/issues/2396/events","html_url":"https://github.com/BryceCurran86/PlanReader-3D/issues/2396","id":5800281675,"node_id":"I_kwDOTZzCC88AAAABWblGSw","number":2396,"title":"GPT MAX: six unresolved Lot16 raster hosts and producer lineage handoff","user":{"login":"BryceCurran86","id":295562166,"node_id":"U_kgDOEZ3rtg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/295562166?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BryceCurran86","html_url":"https://github.com/BryceCurran86","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BryceCurran86/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BryceCurran86/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BryceCurran86/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BryceCurran86/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BryceCurran86/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BryceCurran86/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BryceCurran86/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BryceCurran86/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BryceCurran86/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":862,"created_at":"2026-10-11T10:36:11Z","updated_at":"2026-11-02T05:07:07Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"<!-- GPTMAX-20261015-AUTHORITY-REVIEW-START -->\n## Current original-source authority queue — 2026-10-15\n\n**Production remains21 physical openings /15 authenticated hosts /9 frames /EIGHT accepted signed opening-area quantities. No new accepted quantity, frozen match or accuracy percentage.**\n\nExact first-failure record for all13 existing nonquantity physical objects, isolated STACKER and all9 original raw cases: [ledger6187185325](https://github.com/BryceCurran86/PlanReader-3D/issues/2396#issuecomment-6187185325). Existing8 quantity/customer bodies, original signed lineage,20k cap and frozen truth/evaluator are preserved.\n\n| Task | Verified source outcome / first remaining gate |\n|---|---|\n| STACKER | [DRAFT #2776](https://github.com/BryceCurran86/PlanReader-3D/pull/2776), `gptmax/original-paired-wall-faces-shadow-20261015`, head08e4fc7f. Final isolated original replay COMPLETE. Actual3fcb… snapshot preserved,21→22 physical only. Figured2127/2100×2700mm/5.67m² evidence exists; host left source primitive unmapped; no frame/quantity. Strict full-state retention FAILS at hostless a68 representative119ef8…→399619…, same ABSTAIN/reasons; no waiver. All15 old positive hosts,9 frames,8 quantity/customer bodies and audit seal exact. |\n| STACKER source verification | Exact-head original source38699699963 SUCCESS, both3.13/3.14 negatives SUCCESS. Artifact11956221199 downloaded/inspected; ZIP SHA `08c03ae7a86cbc771a0fae7d8e6460b15619128db140aa1bbb34fd5cb75e1d54`; ENTIRE artifact exactly equals local fresh replay, assertions rerun. FullCI38699699972 and applicable sibling checks still being verified. Earlier genuine new b9d… root/input expansion is retained as failed retention and incomplete frame; never aliased. |\n| BIFOLD | [#2773](https://github.com/BryceCurran86/PlanReader-3D/pull/2773)8.82m² arithmetic/seal hypothesis remains **UNPUBLISHED / SEMANTIC RELEASE BLOCKED** by [GPT1 review6186538797](https://github.com/BryceCurran86/PlanReader-3D/pull/2773#issuecomment-6186538797). New [DRAFT #2779](https://github.com/BryceCurran86/PlanReader-3D/pull/2779) original native role audit authenticates6596 source words/506 queried-block receipts. Exact2142/BIFOLD trusted, but independent door/window filling role absent. Every exported p3 legend word retains `text_clip_state_unresolved` ABSTAIN. Manufacturer/energy/elevation source supplies no exact model/tag role receipt. Native-only snapshot3be147… is distinct; no source/physical identity transfer.68 focused native source tests pass; exact-head original/full CI pending. |\n| Six old unhosted |33d,81a,a68,b248,ba7,f819 individually retain unmapped-side/structural-membership/equivalence gates. Positive local paint/candidate W4 cannot substitute for structural role. Full negative jamb/face evidence retained; no proximity or other-opening host transfer. |\n| Exact incidence |#2770/#2771 all applicable exact-head workflows green. All1162 painted source spans conserved in experimental graph. Claude independent technical COMMENT confirms default original Maryborough W2–W5 hashes unchanged; no formal authority promotion. Lower a68 T remains candidate-only; genuine13/14 and128/130 source negatives preserved. |\n| Frames/metrics |3 hosted nonquantity cases fail aligned-fragment distinctness; four framed nonquantity cases have BIFOLD/SQ.SET kind or missing owned second axis. Single870/1200, generic joinery datum and custom-front measure-on-site evidence do not supply full area. Existing3 figured-area quantities without full frames remain valid and unchanged. |\n| Opening universe |Original selected closure30raw/21resolved/9unresolved; isolated shadow30/22/8. Every original raw case has its own first gate in ledger; both universes incomplete. Four groups outside one authentic plan are not proven globally nonphysical. Count ABSTAIN, no default1. CRNR STACK still lacks physical partition/structural-host/frame proof. |\n| Producer handoff |#2766 exact-head74d0ddc8 source/full CI green, original artifact11950790899 verified; source record handoff supplied at [#2297 comment6185049137](https://github.com/BryceCurran86/PlanReader-3D/issues/2297#issuecomment-6185049137). Selected3fcb…/allpage7ad8…/native3be147… roots remain distinct. GPT3 versioned signed consumer binding open; no self-attested signature or V1 rewrite. |\n\nGPT1/GPT3 received final verified source-stage handoffs [6187156423](https://github.com/BryceCurran86/PlanReader-3D/issues/2017#issuecomment-6187156423) / [6187156729](https://github.com/BryceCurran86/PlanReader-3D/issues/2004#issuecomment-6187156729), with explicit no-new-quantity status. Independent technical review requested. Blocked cases are retained individually while independent source paths are checked; green diagnostic CI is not commercial completion.\n<!-- GPTMAX-20261015-AUTHORITY-REVIEW-END -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- GPTMAX-20261015-BIFOLD-START -->\n## Historical BIFOLD hypothesis — superseded by semantic release block\n\n#2773's isolated8.82m² publisher/seal arithmetic pathway and actual source/host/frame/native/figured receipts are archived at [GPT1 packet6186276179](https://github.com/BryceCurran86/PlanReader-3D/issues/2017#issuecomment-6186276179). Independent GPT1 review6186538797 BLOCKS DOOR-vs-WINDOW semantics. #2779 fresh original audit retains that limitation. This is NOT an authenticated additional construction quantity, a new accepted frozen match, or commercial activation. Existing8 remain accepted. Axis order unresolved and count ABSTAIN. Use the current exact first-failure ledger above.\n<!-- GPTMAX-20261015-BIFOLD-END -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- GPTMAX-20261015-SOURCE-INCIDENCE-START -->\n## Latest source-incidence continuation — 2026-10-15\n\n**No ninth quantity, new authenticated host, complete count or new frozen match.** Main remains `40d8e84913d927e90cda05b5a94d1ffb92d6d574`; original **21 physical records /15 hosts /9 frames /8 accepted quantity/customer rows** are preserved.\n\n- DRAFT [#2770](https://github.com/BryceCurran86/PlanReader-3D/pull/2770), exact head `97d0e3bbb0c305819312fe1476fd73a8881041cb`: fixes same-direction source-overlap cancellation and exact-zero endpoint centroid drift only behind independent explicit shadow flags. Fresh original PDF and source CI [38691884887](https://github.com/BryceCurran86/PlanReader-3D/actions/runs/38691884887) passed; artifact11952387464 downloaded, SHA `ea4a6330724cb688dfa01e1a4685ede50b8d963e3d1d0cbdb710cdbd056afeea`, original sealed/customer receipts independently equal the local replay. Painted source conservation **1088/1162→1162/1162**, not a benchmark/quantity gain. Full CI38691884647 SUCCESS; remaining applicable source jobs being checked.\n- Separate stacked DRAFT [#2771](https://github.com/BryceCurran86/PlanReader-3D/pull/2771), head `7fa6340743d8c90d373607b287b4c3901317b00c`: exact collinear endpoint partitioning with full primitive ancestry, unchanged W3/W4 rules, no offset/rounding/tolerance inference. Fresh original PDF local replay and committed workflow assertions passed; **232 focused tests passed**. All four preceding graph scopes and complete eight quantity/seal/customer receipts exactly retained. Exact-head CI/source artifact pending.\n- Actual a68 upper flank now has continuous source candidate membership. Lower source overlap becomes a candidate T in the additional partitioned graph; the preceding graph's AMBIGUOUS/ABSTAINED result is retained. **The opposite full-sheet jamb1356=13/14 and face1499=128/130 solid original cells remain source negatives**, so they never enter this positive W2 universe. The existing opening-local paint check has a different predicate and does not override those negatives. Structural wall role/ordinary-source membership/equivalence and independent second metric axis are still unproved.\n- [Complete first-stage ledger for all 13 nonquantity objects](https://github.com/BryceCurran86/PlanReader-3D/blob/7fa6340743d8c90d373607b287b4c3901317b00c/docs/engineering/gptmax_exact_collinear_partition_shadow_20261015.md): **six host-wall gates, three frame gates, four metric-axis/vertical gates**. Three existing figured-area quantities independently lack complete frames and remain accepted.\n- Original producer selected snapshot `source_snapshot_3fcb6bc5c44b51d930e9600080501d27`; separate all-page replay `source_snapshot_7ad8bf09e3ebbec9797df89842574683`; original decision scope `wall-source:page-3`. No snapshot/ownership alias or source-only candidate self-certification. #2766/#2297 signed consumer review remains OPEN.\n- Raw closure remains **30 raw /21 resolved /9 unresolved**. No count=1. All original native/raster opposition, ABSTAIN, ambiguous-host results, source PDFs,20k raster cap, frozen V2 reference/evaluator and production/customer output are unchanged. Both PRs require independent review before authority promotion.\n\n**User definition of done remains unmet: NEW physical opening→canonical measurement→GPT1 quantity→GPT3 independent frozen reconciliation. These source corrections do not authorize publication.**\n<!-- GPTMAX-20261015-SOURCE-INCIDENCE-END -->\n\n---\n\n## Earlier source checkpoint retained below\n\n## Current original-source checkpoint — 2026-10-15\n\n**Six physical raster hosts remain unproved. No ninth quantity or new benchmark match is claimed.** Current main `40d8e849` retains **21 physical openings / 15 authenticated hosts / 9 frames / 8 accepted quantity/customer rows**. Older seven-host and 14-host figures below are historical.\n\nCurrent source-only handoff: DRAFT [#2766](https://github.com/BryceCurran86/PlanReader-3D/pull/2766), head `74d0ddc8743df8236181e2acb0b3b26c5ab025bf`. Both Python3.13/3.14 source tests and original immutable-source workflow [38685829450](https://github.com/BryceCurran86/PlanReader-3D/actions/runs/38685829450) SUCCESS. Original artifact [11950790899](https://github.com/BryceCurran86/PlanReader-3D/actions/runs/38685829450/artifacts/11950790899) downloaded and inspected; ZIP SHA `da364e7d31efaec8999adffd5fcac4afa433d56a5b50da2a23297c56e6ab975e`. Full CI38685829362 SUCCESS: Python3.13 and3.14 each14259 passed,55 skipped,13 xfailed. Performance and raster workflows also SUCCESS; all four applicable workflows green. Independent source/consumer review remains pending; no merge/promotion inferred.\n\n### Exact six-host first-stage ledger\nIDs below have prefix `physical_opening_existence_`. Every case retains `no_authenticated_host_wall_band`; right source primitive unmapped for 81a45c, left unmapped for the other five.\n\n| Physical identity suffix | First source/structural gate | Independently reissued label evidence |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 33d277d4c6b6ce758b0594f9d47ce4d8 | Both candidate flanks painted; no ordinary W4 same-source ancestry/structural identity. Original terminal centre span3.84pt stays below unchanged4pt production gate. | Single870 figure; no area or independently witness-bound second axis. |\n| 81a45c3a33c2a4c0bfdf243aa45a780d | Both candidate flanks painted; right ordinary source membership/structural wall/equivalence unproved. | Single870 figure; no area. |\n| a68d0b7d738b5de9a1588b4e680e1a8f | Both candidate flanks painted; exact W3 short-arm junctions remain AMBIGUOUS/ABSTAINED; no ordinary W4 corroboration or transfer of hosted1215 identity. | Single870 figure; no area. |\n| b248972669988c108ebc90c6ca3908fd | First whole-source flank not solid; separate contained terminal0.24pt remains below existing source gate. | Source label unavailable. |\n| ba7f75a2e5f68bcce87cd00ac1acf90b | First whole-source flank not solid; separate76.8pt contained original terminal still lacks structural role/equivalence/host. | Single870 figure; no area. |\n| f819752382d44a00d9f28feca4b00787 | Both candidate flanks painted; ordinary W4 same-source ancestry and structural identity/equivalence unproved. | Label AMBIGUOUS. |\n\nAll 21 retain exact host/frame/measurement traces. Quantity delivery currently partitions into **8 existing quantities**, **6 host gates**, **3 frame gates on nonquantity objects**, **4 metric-axis/vertical gates on already framed objects**. Physical geometry is independently incomplete: six authenticated hosts lack frames, but **three of those retain valid existing figured-area quantities**. Never revoke those areas or pretend they have complete axis-resolved void geometry.\n\n### Producer lineage handoff for #2297\nThe reader accepts original PDF bytes plus source page selectors; it internally replays original source/host/frame/canonical/quantity producers, re-proves physical source existence and reissues original figured-label evidence. It copies actual producer-issued `snapshot_id`, `decision_scope_id`, physical/host/frame record bodies and existing quantity/measurement IDs. Negative producer traces and attempted selectors remain separate from positive host records. Portable JSON is **UNSIGNED/UNPUBLISHED**, `signed_scope_verified=false`; V1 signatures are unchanged.\n\n- Original PDF SHA `10109b4b6e85e6e27af81f6399ce4b92abfdba80f87dc69dd5887bd6f3a65844`.\n- Actual selected p3 decode root: `source_snapshot_3fcb6bc5c44b51d930e9600080501d27`.\n- Separate all13-pages decoded / p3 topology root: `source_snapshot_7ad8bf09e3ebbec9797df89842574683`.\n- Both use revision `source_revision_31b112fa62447a99d83fe3d10044d2bb`; do not alias the two snapshots.\n- Current selected-root replay independently equals the fresh accepted GitHub archive11929406140 for all21 canonical records, eight complete quantities, full original V1 seal and all8 customer rows. Existing seal fingerprint `ef58f8ae1a963a5b985edfa6dda752f3f338d9d5c42d56969b0e86f538aadfeb`.\n- Exact selected-source quantity/physical/host/measurement packet: [#2297 comment6185049137](https://github.com/BryceCurran86/PlanReader-3D/issues/2297#issuecomment-6185049137); GPT3 handoff [comment6185049316](https://github.com/BryceCurran86/PlanReader-3D/issues/2004#issuecomment-6185049316); GPT1 [comment6185052239](https://github.com/BryceCurran86/PlanReader-3D/issues/2017#issuecomment-6185052239).\n- Independent source/measurement/consumer review and GPT3's versioned signed-consumer contract remain OPEN.\n\n### Separate count and raw-source gates\nOriginal #2765 source workflow38684640994 and full CI SUCCESS; inspected artifact11950095147. Raw group7c32fd8f has a genuinely source-painted contiguous41-cell/9.60pt original endpoint, while the original whole-source41/43 ink failure is retained. This is source-only, not an opening/host/height proof. Raw page closure remains **30 raw /21 resolved /9 unresolved**; count completeness is unproved. No count=1, scope subtraction, physical-nonexistence inference or identity transfer. Two historical native lookalikes retain source-owned opposition and ABSTAIN.\n\nOriginal PDFs, accepted identities/quantities, W3 ambiguity, global2.5pt W2 snap,20,000 input primitive cap, W10 and frozen Full Plan V2 truth/evaluator/denominators/tolerances are unchanged. **Definition of done remains a NEW source-supported physical opening → canonical/measurement → GPT1 quantity → GPT3 independent frozen reconciliation; not achieved by this lineage handoff.**\n\n---\n\n## Historical checkpoints retained below (superseded where they conflict with the checkpoint above)\n\n## Current source-verified checkpoint — 2026-10-12\n\n**Seven raster hosts remain unproven.** Current original production is **21 positive opening hypotheses / 14 authenticated hosts / 9 frames**. The historical two native lookalikes retain complete source-owned dimension/fill opposition and remain ABSTAIN; neither is physical nonexistence proof. Older 23-positive totals and draft/merge references below are historical.\n\nVerified #2454 merged at `4fca39791d3b8d88515802b112f52ce8ee3ed535` after all 24 applicable checks, including original Lot16/Maryborough retention and full source replay. #2477 (`92b593871a2324828b377de7847637739fd79a93`) is implemented and freshly source-replayed, but remains DRAFT pending all applicable CI. W3 already has raw-node-index identities; W4's position lookup overwrote them. New shadow lookup requires unique actual incidence and retains coincident/non-simple chains as negative evidence. Eight abstained chains retain 27 actual fragments; no constructor guard, source cap, physical host or quantity gate is weakened.\n\nAll 81 required associations retain complete W3 spans and experimental membership; 78 have a common candidate address across the full interval. Structural role, raster viewport ownership and physical equivalence remain unproved. Eighteen associations still fail a single-fragment contact predicate. Forty-two W4 candidate addresses remain reused; no alternative is silently overwritten or elected.\n\nFive already-hosted openings still lack complete frames. All 21 width traces need witness topology; all 21 height/schedule/vertical traces lack a contained tag binding. Native and raster universes remain incomplete (125/0 and 30/21 raw/resolved); no count=1 or completeness is inferred. Eight canonical records have figured-area metadata, not a verified bijection to the historical eight sealed quantities.\n\nExact source/canonical identities, receipts, frame/metric/count first gates and independent raw-discovery blockers are committed in documentation-only #2485. #2428 remains blocked: current-base source-positive receipts are equal, but native candidates 125 -> 189 and semantic inventory changes; no comparison is waived. #2420 remains blocked by the actual Maryborough grid-area failure. #2144/#2077 remain preserved until verified integration.\n\nFrozen V2 truth/denominators/evaluator/tolerances, W10 and the 20,000 input cap are unchanged. No new host or accuracy gain claimed.\n\n---\n\n## Historical evidence ledger (retained, superseded by checkpoint above)\n\n## GPT MAX original-source nine-case closure ledger — 2026-10-11\nOriginal **byte-verified** Lot16 PDF: `10109b4b6e85e6e27af81f6399ce4b92abfdba80f87dc69dd5887bd6f3a65844`, page 3. Original production: **23 physical opening claims, 14 authenticated hosts, 9 authenticated frames**; no proof of complete physical opening universe, no benchmark/quantity increase. The distinct nine raw raster candidates (30 registered, 21 individually resolved) are NOT these nine physical opening identities.\n\n### Seven source-backed raster physical existences still unhosted — earlier rejected-component-only evidence\nAll IDs have prefix `physical_opening_existence_`:\n- [ ] `2b2a91e8afaf8b7e9a3e07605a80a4a9` — left source primitive missing, **0** rejected-component run matches its left flank (also 0 on right).\n- [ ] `33d277d4c6b6ce758b0594f9d47ce4d8` — left source primitive missing; **2** original positive-pixel runs: `[581,363]-[585,363]` and `[581,363.5]-[585.5,363.5]`; their actual shadow W2 edges `split_6131` and `split_21591` are both **W3 removed**, neither has a W4 owner. Right side had one *ordinary* authenticated source/W4 candidate. Never copy removed ancestry onto unrelated retained edges.\n- [ ] `81a45c3a33c2a4c0bfdf243aa45a780d` — right source primitive missing, **6** positive pixel-run matches; W2 has both removed and retained source edges; retained W4 alternatives include `wall_ff0035842ff75f2870f6` and branched `wall_bebc0140c3bcb0592875`; local wall identity/whole source band NOT proven.\n- [ ] `a68d0b7d738b5de9a1588b4e680e1a8f` — left source primitive missing, **0** rejected-component run matches its required flank (also zero on right).\n- [ ] `b248972669988c108ebc90c6ca3908fd` — left source primitive missing, **0** rejected-component run matches either flank.\n- [ ] `ba7f75a2e5f68bcce87cd00ac1acf90b` — left source primitive missing, **0** matching positive rejected-component runs on left (eight independent run witnesses exist only on the opposite right flank).\n- [ ] `f819752382d44a00d9f28feca4b00787` — left source primitive missing, **6** positive pixel-run matches; shares vertical original-positive ink and experimental W4 alternatives with `81a45c3a...`; physical association remains ambiguous.\n\n### Two non-raster hostless hypotheses — review opening existence rather than invent hosts\n- [ ] `415d34ddc0c7591b181ddadc11aefe1d`: native candidate geometry `[1011.12,450.72]-[1011.12,442.20]` appears on original drawing's 90/450 **dimension annotations**, not within an authenticated wall aperture. Require complete source-owned dimension component opposition; visual proximity alone must NOT delete original candidate or assign a host.\n- [ ] `b222d5310a7df1d632d5daab1a676645`: native candidate geometry `[821.40,730.80]-[720.12,730.80]` lies on **AREA CALCULATIONS** title table. Original PDF paint command `seqno=1682` is fill-only pale neutral `(0.960784,0.960784,0.960784)`, two rectangles `y721.56..730.80` and `740.04..749.28`, no stroke. Generic strict opposing-fill source proof proposed in draft #2395. Must validate all 6 candidate support ownership and retain old host/frame identities before closing as an opposed false positive.\n\n### Required autonomous engineering gates\n1. Original-source #2356 pixel producer **merged** at `c1953a55e4a54a8f0e0ff7b03d5ca9257f302ef2`, original Lot16 source/retention CI passed. Read-only original detector disposition #2340 **merged** at `d4e135bf8a913e66e3b05452422832ebe63d295a`.\n2. Complete exact-source cross-report pixel/G17/W2/W4 join #2361 (currently draft); the first source run failed because ten actual W2 snap-loss fragments lack source parents; corrected to retain them as **negative** evidence, no borrowing lineage, and derived-fragment inventory size kept separate from 20,000 input primitive safety cap. Re-run gate.\n3. For three missing-source sides with positive runs, prove source wall-role visibility, actual surviving W2 geometry, W3 provenance and unambiguous **local physical W4 ownership**; do not elect first/nearest candidate. For other four, use original/source-positive detector discovery without inventing pixels.\n4. For false native candidates, authenticate complete opposing PDF annotation/table paint-role source and retain raw hypotheses as unresolved; do not claim physical nonexistence from visual inspection.\n5. Before ANY source-producer/host merge require exact original Lot16 14 host and nine frame receipt preservation and Maryborough source parity. Do not merge #2364 if Maryborough grid regression is failing.\n6. No frozen V2 manifest/reference/denominator/evaluator/tolerance modification, no guessed wall, geometry or opening count, no published quantity without source authority and never relax the 20,000 input primitive cap.\n\n## Dependencies\n#2356 (merged), #2340 (merged), #2361 (draft, source audit), #2395 (draft, native neutral-fill source opposition), #2364 (draft, original Maryborough grid regression BLOCKED), rejected source-loss experiments #2032 and #2161 (archived, unmerged).\n\n**Done means every case has an independently source-proven legitimate host OR explicitly evidenced non-opening opposition/ABSTAIN, with the complete old source host/frame identity retained, and re-run exact source/benchmark reconciliation. A mere host count of 23 is NOT completion.**\n\n## Current continuation — original-source audit and draft implementation\n\n**No nine-case closure or recovered-host gain is claimed.** The default original control remains 23 claims / 14 authenticated hosts / nine frames. Frozen V2 truth/evaluator/tolerances/denominators and the 20,000 input-primitive cap are unchanged.\n\n- **#2403**, exact head `76675643bb865048d68f74af021866bb56a718fc`: clean-base native pale-neutral fill opposition plus a separate fresh-PDF retention audit. Original source replay is 23→22 claims solely by opposing the unhosted/unframed Area Calculations hypothesis; all 14 host receipts and nine frame receipts are exactly retained. The default strict comparator is unchanged. Four stale source workflow comparisons were corrected; exact-head job `114456830360` exposed the fourth historical positive-universe equality failure, and the revised workflow now independently replays the exact base and reauthenticates the original opposition. Maryborough still requires exact binding/firm-frame parity. Keep draft pending new exact-head source gates.\n- **#2408**, exact head `f7fedb6da0067291fd9a0257e3130fc886795907`: complete original foreground-to-local W2/W3/W4 audit, independently replayed from immutable PDF bytes. All 14 flanks have positive original ink; 6,016 raster runs + 4,083 ordinary source inputs = **10,099 input primitives**, zero unmapped source parents. Derived inventory: 16,409 W2 edges, 46,270 snap-collapsed fragments, 6,013 W3-retained edges and 4,682 W4 records. One W4 address is reused; all alternatives remain explicit, no owner is elected. Remote surviving ancestry never substitutes for lost local geometry.\n- **#2411**, exact head `0431afb45ab66f295e8550fc8a649b0187be529d`: original native text paint partition audit. The 415d dimension hypothesis spans two chains. Four of six supports already have annotation-component coverage; the two lower-chain supports remain uncovered because original word `90450` has an ABSTAINED text-integrity receipt (`text_trace_unavailable`). Source paint commands 954=`90` and 956=`450` are separated by fill-path 955. The audit retains exact glyph/paint ownership and the negative receipt, never feeds untrusted numeric partitions into the component compiler, and leaves the live hypothesis unchanged. **This case remains open.**\n\n### Complete foreground missing-side local disposition\nThese are original run alternatives, not opening objects or recovered hosts. Identity prefix means `physical_opening_existence_`.\n\n| Identity prefix | Required side | No local W2 survivor | Local W3 discard | Local W4 alternative, authority unproved |\n|---|---|---:|---:|---:|\n| `2b2a91e8` | left | 0 | 3 | 2 |\n| `33d277d4` | left | 7 | 0 | 0 |\n| `81a45c3a` | right | 5 | 0 | 0 |\n| `a68d0b7d` | left | 0 | 5 | 1 |\n| `b2489726` | left | 0 | 3 | 2 |\n| `ba7f75a2` | left | 0 | 5 | 3 |\n| `f8197523` | left | 6 | 0 | 0 |\n\nThus three required sides lack locally surviving W2 geometry; four have local W4 alternatives without original structural wall-role, authenticated floor-plan viewport and physical-equivalence authority. The earlier rejected-component-only evidence above remains historical; this fresh complete-foreground audit supersedes its discovery gaps without promoting a host.\n\n### Validation and next gates\n\n74 focused opposition/strict-retention tests, 107 existing source/opening/frame tests, 60 complete-foreground/local-stage tests, and 152 native partition/dimension/text-integrity tests passed. Original PDF source replays and strict existing-host/frame preservation passed locally. Provider isolation, V2 integrity, Ruff F821/F823 and workflow YAML/inline Python checks passed. Source-opposition smoke passed. Its full local suite: **11,190 passed, 51 skipped, 13 xfailed, one schedule-identity failure**, independently reproduced on unchanged `9dc7125`; this is not a passed full-suite claim or a waiver of CI.\n\nAll three PRs remain draft until required exact-head CI/source checks pass. #2395 remains active and overlaps the generic fill-role delta in #2403; reconcile that overlap before integrating either successor. #2364 remains blocked by its Maryborough grid regression. Next source engineering: prove safe source ownership across the intervening native paint at the existing text authority; recover source-owned local W2 fragments in shadow; prove structural role/viewport/equivalence for the surviving W4 alternatives. Do not borrow lineage, relax tolerances/cap, or close a case solely from an ink/host count.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/BryceCurran86/PlanReader-3D/issues/2396/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/BryceCurran86/PlanReader-3D/issues/2396/timeline","performed_via_github_app":{"id":1144995,"client_id":"Iv23liVemv8A9if9v0F2","slug":"chatgpt-codex-connector","node_id":"A_kwHOAOQ6Gs4AEXij","owner":{"login":"openai","id":14957082,"node_id":"MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjE0OTU3MDgy","avatar_ur